(* Pre-Genesis Inscription Grammar, Version 1.
   AuthorityEffect: None. GenesisEffect: None.
   Conforms to check_grammars.py EBNF subset. All productions defined here.

   Scope. A later host notation for selected inscriptions discussed in the
   source transcripts. This grammar was not tested by those model trials.
   The inscription alphabet is
   Sigma_pre = { "<", ">", "a", "b" }: two boundary delimiters and two opaque
   payload glyphs. The regime notation additionally uses braces and commas.
   The Sigma36 glyphs, the
   directed cut "<a->b>" and the admission events of genesis.ebnf and sn.ebnf
   arrive only with Genesis.

   Four states this grammar keeps apart (010 paper, CLAIM-MSSN-001):
     absent input    no document at all; not a word, matched by no start
     empty word      the empty string; refused by every public start
     "<>"            the literal token parsed by this declared host grammar
     ground carrier  the stage object S(0) adopts; not a string at all

   Public starts, in order of growth:
     ground_token        exactly "<>"
     inscription         one balanced, non-nested bracketed inscription
     pre_genesis_regime  zero or more inscriptions between braces; "{}" is the
                         empty host list notation and is not the empty word

   There are no event productions. The first event, supply("<>"), is the
   Genesis boundary and lives in ../../001_genesis/grammar/genesis.ebnf.
   Parsing a word admits no carrier, transition, or observational operation. *)

pre_genesis_regime = "{", [ inscription, { ",", inscription } ], "}" ;

inscription = ground_token | occupied_token ;
ground_token = "<>" ;
occupied_token = "<", payload, ">" ;

payload = payload_glyph, { payload_glyph } ;
payload_glyph = "a" | "b" ;
